                </div>
                <div class="title" data-transid="prodm">Items</div>
              </div>
              <div class="desc">Axi ERP can manage large number of items. Items may comprise of raw materials,
                semi-finished goods, finished goods & consumables. An item is categorized using the item category, item
                sub category & brand.

                Items can be bought in a unit of measure, stored in a different unit of measure and sold in a different
                unit of measure. The inventory can be maintained in primary and secondary units of measure too. This is
                critical in many businesses.




                Each item category and sub category may be associated with a HSN code, purchase account, sales account &
                stock account. Items that belong to a sub category and category are associated with corresponding HSN
                code and GL accounts. The mapping with HSN code or an account can be done at item category, sub category
                or at item level. The mapping done at item level will override the mapping done at sub category level &
                category level. Similarly mapping done at sub category level will override the mapping done at category
                level.





                Use <a>Taxes</a> option to setup the list of taxes applicable.



                Use <a>HSN/SAC</a> code option to view/create HSN codes. Every HSN code is associated with the
                applicable tax code.




                HSN code may be assigned to an item or its sub category or its category. The tax associated with the
                assigned HSN code will be used in all transactions.



                The purchase account, sales account and stock account may be assigned to an item or its sub category or
                its category. The transactions are posted to the assigned account when invoices, purchases and other
                transactions are made for an item.
              </div>


            </div>
